            <ArticleTitle>Does the presence and site of myocardial ischemia on perfusion scintigraphy predict the occurrence and site of future myocardial infarction in patients with stable coronary artery disease?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1521-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In 47 patients who had undergone myocardial scintigraphy, reversible perfusion abnormality was detected in only 28 segments (60%) that were the site of future acute myocardial infarction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
